WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.680
Employers see plenty of claims about AI engineers and very little proof. This directory puts the proof first.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:19.630
This is the live directory. A person appears here only once a case study about work they built is approved and published. No case study, no listing.

3
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:32.880
The page says how a listing is earned, in four steps: real work in a real repository, checked against its criteria, written up as a reviewed case study, and only then listed.

4
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:44.580
Open a profile and the headline figures come from that engineer's published case studies, not from a skills list they typed in. Names in this walkthrough are replaced with a role.

5
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:54.570
Every claim on the profile leads to a published case study like this one: the problem, what was built, how it works, and what it measured.

6
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:07.740
The rule is enforced where the data leaves. A project without a published case study, and the commits from its repository, never leave the server, so there is nothing to find in the page source.

7
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:17.240
An employer who wants to talk asks for an introduction, and the Colaberry team makes it. Candidates' contact details are never shown.

8
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:26.670
Booking is the candidate's switch. While it is off, the schedule page says so plainly and offers the introduction instead.

9
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:40.390
With booking on, the page offers only open times in the candidate's zone. Each request is decided under a lock, then waits for the candidate to accept, suggest another time or decline.

10
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:52.240
Candidates can record an intro video in the browser. The coach measures pace, filler words and voice against published targets, and the face is not analyzed.

11
00:01:53.300 --> 00:02:06.180
Six of six listed engineers have a published case study behind them. Twenty of twenty eight modules have a test file of their own name. All sixteen commits name an AI coding assistant as co-author.

12
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:17.710
Before a fix on fourteen November most visits to the site landed in a catch-all category, and today none do. No listed engineer has switched booking on yet.

13
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:26.830
No interview has been booked, so whether a listing leads to a hire is still unmeasured. The record says so plainly.

14
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:36.280
The directory cannot list anyone without a published case study, and an employer's request waits for the candidate to decide.
